# Bekaa3D frontend environment — the canonical list of every variable the
# frontend reads. Copy to .env.local (git-ignored) for local development.
# No secret ever belongs here: the backend holds every secret (JWT, CSRF,
# TURNSTILE_SECRET, payment and email keys). Production details:
# docs/setup/production-readiness.md.
#
# IMPORTANT: Next.js reads these at BUILD time. NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are
# inlined into the browser bundle by `next build`, and the rewrite rules
# (API_PROXY_TARGET, MEDIA_PROXY_TARGET) are compiled into the build's
# routes manifest. Set them before `npm run build`, not only before
# `npm run start`.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server-only (never NEXT_PUBLIC_; the browser never learns these)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Where `next.config.ts` rewrites same-origin /api/* (and /api/health/*) to.
#   Development: required (the backend on :8000).
#   Production:  leave UNSET when the reverse proxy routes /api/* straight to
#                the backend (the recommended topology: large Bring Your Idea
#                uploads must not pass through Next). Set it only if Next
#                itself must proxy the API, and then know that Next buffers at
#                most 10 MB of a request body, so BYI uploads above that fail.
API_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:8000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Development only (ignored by production builds)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The backend API does not serve /media/* locally (BACKEND-RESPONSE.md B4).
# Run a static server over the backend checkout's storage/media_public folder,
# e.g. from the backend root:  npx serve storage/media_public -l 8001
# Production serves /media from the reverse proxy; this rule is never built
# into a production build.
# MEDIA_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:8001

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public (NEXT_PUBLIC_: inlined into the browser bundle at build time)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Cloudflare Turnstile PUBLIC site key (public by design).
#   Development/test: when unset, falls back to Cloudflare's always-pass test
#                     key 1x00000000000000000000AA, which issues the dummy token
#                     the backend's CAPTCHA_PROVIDER=fake accepts.
#   Production:       REQUIRED. A production build NEVER falls back to the test
#                     key; with no key every captcha form shows "Verification is
#                     unavailable right now" and cannot be submitted.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=1x00000000000000000000AA

# REAL ONLINE PAYMENT IS NOT BUILT (backend VS-032); the only online provider
# is the backend's `mock`. A production build never sends a shopper to the
# mock provider's page. Set this to "true" ONLY in a staging build that must
# exercise the mock payment flow. Never in a public production build.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ALLOW_MOCK_PAYMENTS=false

# NODE_ENV is set by Next itself (`next dev` = development, `next build` /
# `next start` = production). Do not set it by hand.
